{
  "$header": " ============================================================\n   Growth — Design Tokens\n   GENERATED by scripts/generate-tokens.mjs from tokens/tokens.json.\n   DO NOT EDIT BY HAND -- edit tokens.json and re-run the script.\n   (tests/tokens.test.ts fails if this file and the JSON disagree.)\n\n   Source file : b6JvDQQ7QcWJpckvZyAbjm\n   Generated   : 2026-08-26\n   Counts      : 78 primitives · 55 semantic · 24 scale\n\n   Three tiers, and the rule that makes it a system:\n     TIER 1  primitives  — raw values. Never referenced by a component.\n     TIER 2  semantic    — role names. This is the ONLY tier components use.\n     TIER 3  scale       — spacing, radius, border width. Mode-independent.\n\n   A component that reaches past tier 2 into a primitive is a bug.\n   ============================================================ ",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "selector": ":root",
      "notes": [
        " Light-mode contrast, measured rather than judged.\n\n   --text-muted was neutral-400 (#9A9AA6): 2.78:1 on a card, 2.48:1 on\n   page-top, against a WCAG AA requirement of 4.5:1 for body text. It is the\n   colour of every caption, axis label, timestamp and hint in the product --\n   the single most-used text token, and the one that failed hardest.\n\n   The three semantic pairs failed too: good 2.80:1, warn 2.99:1, bad 3.42:1,\n   all at 12px. The dark-mode equivalents pass at 5.6-7.2:1, which is the tell\n   -- the light pairs were never measured, they were matched by eye against a\n   dark comp where the same hues happen to work.\n\n   Fixed by extending the ramps rather than by overriding the semantic layer\n   with hex. green/red/amber jumped 500 -> 900, and 900 renders a status pill\n   nearly black at ~12:1; the new 700 steps hold hue and saturation and land at\n   4.6:1. The tier rule survives: semantics still alias primitives.\n\n   Dark mode's semantic pairs were already fine (5.6-7.2:1) and are untouched.\n   Its --text-muted was NOT -- neutral-500 gives 3.71:1 on a dark card. I wrote\n   \"dark already passes\" in this comment before measuring that specific token,\n   which is the same mistake as every other one recorded in this repo: asserting\n   a property adjacent to the one actually checked. It is neutral-400 now\n   (6.40:1), and the measurement is in the commit rather than the claim. "
      ],
